course: dictionary
lesson: 1704
title: Cicadas: loud singers with a long wait
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cicada is a large insect with clear wings and big eyes. You often hear a cicada before you see one, because males make a very loud buzzing or clicking song in summer. The sentence «Cicadas are among the loudest insects» gives you a clue: loudest tells you they make a lot of noise.
explain: Cicadas have a surprising life story. Young cicadas, called nymphs, live underground for years. Then they climb out, shed their skin and become adults. The empty skins they leave behind can often be found stuck to trees.
explain: Context helps with the word «drum-like» in «males click drum-like plates on their bodies». A drum makes a sound when it is hit, so the plates must make a sound like a drum. Check it by swapping in your meaning: a clicking plate that works like a tiny drum makes sense.
fact: A cicada is a large insect with clear wings and big eyes.
fact: Male cicadas make a very loud buzzing or clicking song in summer.
fact: Young cicadas, called nymphs, live underground for years before they climb out.
fact: When a cicada climbs out, it sheds its skin and leaves an empty shell on a tree.
fact: Some American cicadas, called periodical cicadas, come out all together every 13 or 17 years.
exercise: «Cicadas are among the loudest insects.» What does loudest mean? | *Making the most noise | Hardest to see | Slowest to move | Smallest
exercise: Where do young cicadas, called nymphs, live for years? | In the sea | high up in the tops of tall trees | *Underground | Inside houses
exercise: What is left on a tree after a cicada climbs out and becomes an adult? | A nest of eggs | *An empty skin | A feather | A pile of dry leaves
test: Which statement about male cicadas is true? | *They make a loud buzzing or clicking song in summer | They are silent all year round | They have no wings | They live only in cold places
test: Why are periodical cicadas so special? | They can fly across oceans | *They come out all together every 13 or 17 years | They never leave the ground | They only eat flowers
exam: Read «males click drum-like plates on their bodies». What does drum-like most likely mean? | Soft and fluffy | Shiny and smooth | *Making a sound like a drum | Very tiny
